t-size: 9px;\">Not Detected</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">copies/mL or Ct</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Not Detected</span></td>\n<td><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">No active HSV-2 infection</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1512\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1501\" data-end=\"1510\">Note:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1724\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1625\">\n<p data-start=\"1515\" data-end=\"1625\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">If <em data-start=\"1518\" data-end=\"1528\">Detected</em>, include <strong data-start=\"1538\" data-end=\"1550\">Ct value</strong> (Cycle threshold) and mention \"<strong data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1623\">Positive &ndash; Active Infection Suspected</strong>\".</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1626\" data-end=\"1724\">\n<p data-start=\"1628\" data-end=\"1724\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Values like <code data-start=\"1640\" data-end=\"1649\">Ct &lt; 35</code> often suggest active viral replication (depending on kit &amp; lab protocols).</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
